# --- Lazarus / Free Pascal build output -------------------------------------
lib/
backup/
*.lps
*.compiled
*.ppu
*.or
*.a
*.dbg
link*.res
*.bak
*~

# --- compiled program -------------------------------------------------------
etchasketch
etchasketch.exe

# --- staged builds ----------------------------------------------------------
dist/

# NOTE: etchasketch.res (icon + manifest) and etchasketch.ico are project
# sources, not build output - they are meant to stay in the repository.

# --- editor / OS ------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- never publish -----------------------------------------------------------
# Agent working directories and session state: these hold transcripts, local
# paths and whatever was pasted into them.  None of it belongs in a public
# repository, and none of it has ever been committed here.
.claude/
.codex/
.aider*
CLAUDE.local.md
*-crash.txt

# --- ours, not the world's ---------------------------------------------------
# The report collector and what it collects stay off GitHub.  The script is
# the operator's side of the arrangement, and the reports are other people's
# drawings and words.
tools/
reports/

# --- how the work is done, as opposed to what the work is --------------------
# Agent instructions, the report-collector's operating notes and anything else
# describing the process rather than the program.  A public repository should
# say what the program does; it has no business explaining how the people and
# tools behind it are told to behave.
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.local.md
AGENTS.md
SUGGESTIONS_TO_CLAUDE.md
docs/bug-report-endpoint.md

# a compiled binary that got in here once under a mistyped name
etchasketcdhjsd

# --- the program's own runtime files -----------------------------------------
# It keeps its settings, draft, lock and crash reports next to the executable
# now that it is portable - and during development the executable is right
# here, so all of that lands in the working copy.  None of it belongs in the
# repository: it is one developer's window position and one machine's state.
heckers-sketch.cfg
heckers-sketch.lock
heckers-sketch-draft.hsk*
heckers-sketch-crash.txt*
heckers-sketch-*.download
*.hsk.would-not-open
reports/
